## Repository-Specific Patterns (CRITICAL)

**These patterns MUST be followed exactly for this repository:**

### 1) Model Rule for LIST Responses

**Even if the API returns a list, ALWAYS generate a single ROOT model:**
- Repository method MUST return `Future<RootModel>` (e.g., `Future<ProjectsModel>`)
- NEVER return `Future<List<SomeModel>>` or `Future<Response>`
- The list MUST live inside the root model structure (e.g., `ProjectsModel.data.items`)
- The bloc MUST access the list from the model, NOT from a List return type

**Example Structure:**
```dart
// Repository - CORRECT
static Future<ProjectsModel> getProjects(SearchEngine data) async {
  return await Network().request(
    ApiNames.projects,
    query: data.query,
    method: ServerMethods.POST,
    model: ProjectsModel(),
  );
}

// Bloc - CORRECT
ProjectsModel model = await ProjectsRepo.getProjects(searchData);
List<ProjectItem> items = model.data?.items ?? [];
emit(Done(data: items));

// Repository - WRONG
static Future<List<ProjectItem>> getProjects(params) { return [...]; }
static Future<Response> getProjects(params) { return response; }
```

### 2) Repository Method Wiring Pattern

**All repo methods MUST follow the `Network().request` pattern:**
```dart
static Future<RootModel> methodName(params) async {
  return await Network().request(
    ApiNames.endpointName,
    query: data.query,        // if POST with body
    method: ServerMethods.GET, // or POST, PUT, DELETE
    model: RootModel(),        // REQUIRED: pass empty instance
  );
}
```

**Rules:**
- Return type: `Future<RootModel>` (NOT `Future<Response>`, NOT `Future<dynamic>`)
- Always use `Network().request()` (NOT direct Dio calls)
- Always pass `model: RootModel()` parameter
- Use `ServerMethods.GET`, `ServerMethods.POST`, etc. (NOT lowercase strings)

### 3) Model Generation from JSON Response

**When the response has wrapper structure (succeeded, data, validationErrors), generate at minimum:**

**For single-object endpoints:**
```dart
class FeatureModel extends SingleMapper {
  bool? succeeded;
  FeatureDataModel? data;
  dynamic warningErrors;
  List<dynamic>? validationErrors;

  FeatureModel({this.succeeded, this.data, this.warningErrors, this.validationErrors});

  FeatureModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    succeeded = json['succeeded'];
    data = json['data'] != null ? FeatureDataModel.fromJson(json['data']) : null;
    warningErrors = json['warningErrors'];
    validationErrors = json['validationErrors'] != null ? List<dynamic>.from(json['validationErrors']) : null;
  }

  @override
  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {
    final Map<String, dynamic> data = <String, dynamic>{};
    data['succeeded'] = succeeded;
    if (this.data != null) data['data'] = this.data!.toJson();
    data['warningErrors'] = warningErrors;
    if (validationErrors != null) data['validationErrors'] = validationErrors;
    return data;
  }

  @override
  Mapper fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    return FeatureModel.fromJson(json);
  }
}

class FeatureDataModel {
  int? id;
  String? title;
  // Direct fields from data object

  FeatureDataModel({this.id, this.title});

  FeatureDataModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    id = json['id'];
    title = json['title'];
  }

  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {
    final Map<String, dynamic> data = <String, dynamic>{};
    data['id'] = id;
    data['title'] = title;
    return data;
  }
}
```

**For list endpoints:**
```dart
class FeaturesModel extends SingleMapper {
  bool? succeeded;
  FeaturesDataModel? data;
  dynamic warningErrors;
  List<dynamic>? validationErrors;

  FeaturesModel({this.succeeded, this.data, this.warningErrors, this.validationErrors});

  FeaturesModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    succeeded = json['succeeded'];
    data = json['data'] != null ? FeaturesDataModel.fromJson(json['data']) : null;
    warningErrors = json['warningErrors'];
    validationErrors = json['validationErrors'] != null ? List<dynamic>.from(json['validationErrors']) : null;
  }

  @override
  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {
    final Map<String, dynamic> data = <String, dynamic>{};
    data['succeeded'] = succeeded;
    if (this.data != null) data['data'] = this.data!.toJson();
    data['warningErrors'] = warningErrors;
    if (validationErrors != null) data['validationErrors'] = validationErrors;
    return data;
  }

  @override
  Mapper fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    return FeaturesModel.fromJson(json);
  }
}

class FeaturesDataModel {
  List<FeatureItemModel>? items;
  int? currentPage;
  int? pageSize;
  int? totalPages;
  int? totalCount;
  bool? isLastPage;

  FeaturesDataModel({this.items, this.currentPage, this.pageSize, this.totalPages, this.totalCount, this.isLastPage});

  FeaturesDataModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    if (json['items'] != null) {
      items = <FeatureItemModel>[];
      json['items'].forEach((v) {
        items!.add(FeatureItemModel.fromJson(v));
      });
    }
    currentPage = json['currentPage'];
    pageSize = json['pageSize'];
    totalPages = json['totalPages'];
    totalCount = json['totalCount'];
    isLastPage = json['isLastPage'];
  }

  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {
    final Map<String, dynamic> data = <String, dynamic>{};
    if (items != null) data['items'] = items!.map((v) => v.toJson()).toList();
    data['currentPage'] = currentPage;
    data['pageSize'] = pageSize;
    data['totalPages'] = totalPages;
    data['totalCount'] = totalCount;
    data['isLastPage'] = isLastPage;
    return data;
  }
}

class FeatureItemModel {
  int? id;
  String? title;
  // Each item's fields

  FeatureItemModel({this.id, this.title});

  FeatureItemModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    id = json['id'];
    title = json['title'];
  }

  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {
    final Map<String, dynamic> data = <String, dynamic>{};
    data['id'] = id;
    data['title'] = title;
    return data;
  }
}
```

**Rules:**
- Root model extends `SingleMapper` and implements `fromJson(Map<String, dynamic>)` method
- Always include `succeeded`, `warningErrors`, `validationErrors` if present in response
- For paginated lists, create a separate Data model that holds `items` + pagination fields
- For nested objects, create dedicated model classes

### 4) Bloc & States File Naming

**CRITICAL: This repo uses this pattern:**
- Create `<feature_slug>_bloc.dart` (uses shared AppEvent from core)
- Create `<feature_slug>_states.dart` (custom states or use shared AppState)
- Do NOT create `<feature_slug>_event.dart` file (we use shared AppEvent pattern)
- Do NOT create `part` directives for events

**Example Bloc:**
```dart
// latest_request_bloc.dart
import 'package:pms_system/latest_request/model/latest_request_models.dart';
import 'package:pms_system/latest_request/repo/latest_request_repo.dart';
import 'package:pms_system/shared/pms_exports.dart';

class LatestRequestBloc extends Bloc<AppEvent, AppState> {
  LatestRequestBloc() : super(Start()) {
    on<Click>(_onClick);
  }

  _onClick(AppEvent event, Emitter<AppState> emit) async {
    try {
      emit(Loading());
      
      LatestRequestModel model = await LatestRequestRepo.getLatestRequest();
      
      emit(Done(model: model));
    } catch (e) {
      AppCore.errorMessage(allTranslations.text('something_went_wrong'));
      emit(Error());
    }
  }
}
```

**Example States (if custom needed):**
```dart
// latest_request_states.dart
abstract class LatestRequestState {}

class LatestRequestInitial extends LatestRequestState {}

class LatestRequestLoading extends LatestRequestState {}

class LatestRequestLoaded extends LatestRequestState {
  final LatestRequestModel model;
  LatestRequestLoaded(this.model);
}

class LatestRequestError extends LatestRequestState {
  final String message;
  LatestRequestError(this.message);
}
```

## Strict Enforcement

**These rules are in addition to the HARD ENFORCEMENT RULES at the top of this document.**

- **NEVER ask multiple questions at once** - Only ONE question mark per response
- **NEVER use bullet lists in questions** - Single question format only
- **NEVER add prefacing text** like "reviewing", "to proceed", "I will"
- **ALWAYS include ONE example answer inline** in each question
- **NEVER proceed to next question without user's answer**
- **NEVER skip questions** - ask all questions in exact sequence
- **ALWAYS implement work immediately after each answer group** (follow phase rules)
- **ALWAYS wait for explicit user response** before continuing
- **NEVER create or update AI markdown spec files** during workflow
- **NEVER refer to non-existent paths** - only refer to real paths detected in the repo
- **After each user answer:** respond with ONE short confirmation sentence (no lists), perform the phase work immediately, then ask the next single question with example
- **After each phase implementation:** briefly mention what was created
- **Never say "reviewing project" or provide multi-option lists** - embed options naturally if needed, still only one question

## Mode Lock Enforcement

**Mode stays LOCKED throughout the entire workflow:**
- Once mode is set (FEATURE, DESIGN, or BOTH), it stays fixed
- Only way to change mode:
  - User explicitly types: "switch to feature" OR "switch to design" OR "switch to both"
  - User explicitly types: "cancel create" OR "reset create"
  - User starts a completely new trigger
- If `mode = FEATURE`, do NOT mention design or both steps at all
- If `mode = DESIGN`, do NOT mention feature or both steps at all
- If `mode = BOTH`, do NOT mention feature or design separately

## Verify Gates (Silent Self-Check)

**After each phase implementation, silently verify (do NOT show reasoning to user):**

**After PHASE 1 (Scaffolding):**
- feature_root computed once, no duplicates created
- bloc folder contains exactly: `<feature_slug>_bloc.dart` and `<feature_slug>_states.dart`
- NO `<feature_slug>_event.dart` file exists
- All required folders created: `bloc/`, `model/`, `repo/`, `view/`, `widgets/`
- All placeholder files created successfully
- Navigation/routing added
- If any check fails, fix immediately before asking next question

**After PHASE 2 (API Info):**
- Endpoint constant added to api_names.dart
- No premature repo method creation (wait for Q4)

**After PHASE 3 (Models & Logic for FEATURE or BOTH):**
- Root model created with proper structure (extends SingleMapper)
- Repo method return type is `Future<RootModel>` (NOT Response, NOT dynamic)
- Repo uses `Network().request(... model: RootModel())`
- Bloc uses RootModel and reads items from model structure (for lists: `model.data?.items`)
- Bloc emits typed states
- If any check fails, fix immediately before proceeding

**After PHASE 4 (UI for BOTH):**
- Real UI implemented (not just placeholder)
- All strings extracted to localization
- Theme/design system patterns followed
- UI wired to Bloc correctly
- If any check fails, fix immediately before completing

